@startuml
' Card selection modes -- synchronous vs. asynchronous (informative)

' == THEME (activity) ==

!define C_YELLOW FEFECE
!define C_RED    FDEDEC
!define C_PURPLE F4ECF7
!define C_BLUE   EBF5FB
!define C_GREEN  E9F7EF
!define C_GREY   EAECEE
!define C_GREY1  F8F9F9

skinparam defaultTextAlignment center

skinparam activity {
    BackgroundColor #C_GREEN
    BackgroundColor<<blue>>   #C_BLUE
    BackgroundColor<<yellow>>  #C_YELLOW
    BackgroundColor<<red>>    #C_RED
    BackgroundColor<<purple>> #C_PURPLE
    BackgroundColor<<grey>>   #C_GREY
    hide <<blue>> stereotype
    hide <<yellow>> stereotype
    hide <<red>> stereotype
    hide <<purple>> stereotype
    hide <<grey>> stereotype
    DiamondBackgroundColor #C_YELLOW
}

' == CONTENT ==

|#C_GREY1|Card reader A| Card Reader
|Application|
|#C_GREY1|Card reader B| Card Reader
|Event handler|
|Application|
start
:**prepareSelection()**
build the card selection scenario;
if (selection mode?) then (synchronous)
  :**processCardSelectionScenario()**
  or
  **processMultichannelCardSelectionScenario()**;
  |Card reader A|
  :execute the scenario
  on the already-present card;
  |Application|
  :receive **CardSelectionResult**;
  :process the card;
  stop
else (asynchronous)
  :**scheduleCardSelectionScenario()**;
  :**startCardDetection()**;
  |Card reader B|
  :wait for a card, then execute
  the scheduled scenario on insertion;
  :notify **CardReaderEvent**
  **CARD_MATCHED** / **CARD_INSERTED**
  (per **CardPresenceNotificationPolicy**);
  |Event handler|
  :**parseScheduledCardSelectionsResponse()**;
  :process the card;
  :**endCardProcessing()**;
  stop
endif
@enduml
